{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"Swidux-logo","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is a Redux-style state-management library for SwiftUI. State lives in one observable store, mutations go through reducers, and side effects run as async effects. Macros generate the observability boilerplate. Built-in plugins handle persistence and undo\/redo. Optional plugins ship ready-made paywalls (RevenueCat or StoreKit-shaped), version killswitches, parental gates, analytics (Mixpanel or any backend), feature flags, and SwiftData\/iCloud persistence.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The dispatch cycle:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["View → store.send(.action)","  → willReduce hooks (UndoPlugin snapshots here)","  → reducer mutates state in place, optionally returns Effect","  → plugin reducers handle their own actions","  → afterReduce hooks (PersistencePlugin drains EntityStore changelogs here)","  → observer tree updates only changed properties (per-property observation)","  → effects run on a background actor; results dispatch back via @MainActor send"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Your domain types and database stay in your app. Swidux provides the contracts, observability, and dispatch loop.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Companion-Packages","text":"Companion Packages","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Vendor-specific adapters live in their own repositories so a third-party SDK never enters the core dependency graph. Each ships a drop-in service conformer plus a preview mock, and publishes its own DocC reference:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxRevenueCatPaywall\/documentation\/swiduxrevenuecatpaywall\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — RevenueCat adapter for the paywall plugin ("},{"code":"RevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"MockRevenueCatPaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and the "},{"code":"SwiduxRevenueCatPaywallUI","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sheet). See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginPaywallReference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/heirloomlogic.github.io\/SwiduxMixpanelAnalytics\/documentation\/swiduxmixpanelanalytics\/","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" — Mixpanel adapter for the analytics plugin ("},{"code":"MixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"MockMixpanelAnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginAnalyticsReference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","externalID":"Swidux","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"collection","title":"Swidux","roleHeading":"Framework"},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Tutorials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Buildin